+ * +0xc height, +0x10 pixel format, +0x14 bytes per element, +0x18 bytes per
+ * row; layout read off iOS 16.7.16's IOSurfaceClientWrapClientImage) and
+ * IOSurfaceWrapClientMemory (7: scalars address, size): a surface made of the
+ * caller's own memory. CoreAnimation's GL renderer wraps images so, app icons
+ * among them (G4 run gl4: icons missing while 0123 refused these calls). The
+ * range stays prepared (wired) for as long as the surface lives; every task
+ * maps it as usual. From topaz (MakrSas/ios-topaz) 0132, APSL 2.0.
+ */
+IOReturn
+IOSurfaceRootUserClient::wrapClient(uint32_t selector, IOExternalMethodArguments *args)
+{
+	uint64_t address, size;
+	uint32_t width, height, format = 0, bpe, bpr;
